          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കടത്തുവള്ളം — kaṭattuvaḷḷaṁ — \"a ferry boat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഗ്രാമത്തിലുള്ളവർ കടത്തുവള്ളത്തിൽ പുഴ കടക്കുന്നു. grāmattiluḷḷavar kaṭattuvaḷḷattil puḻa kaṭakkunnu. The villagers cross the river in a ferry boat."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കടത്ത് is a crossing, from കടക്കുക, to cross; the ferryman is the കടത്തുകാരൻ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കടത്തുവള്ളം (kaṭattuvaḷḷaṁ) is a native Dravidian compound of കടത്ത്, a carrying across (DEDR 1109), and വള്ളം, a boat (DEDR 5315)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
